card.statement:
Given $x\in\mathcal{S}^{0}$, $v\in T_n(\mathbb C)$ and $\Delta\subsetneq \Sigma$, we define an element $v_{\Delta}\in T_{n}(\mathbb{C})$ whose $(ij)$-th component is

$$
(v_{\Delta})_{ij}=
\begin{cases}
x_{ij}, &  \text{ if }\ \ \ \ \ \  (i,j)\notin\{(k_{r},i_{r}),(k_{r},j_{r}) \; | \; r \in \Delta \}\\
v_{ij}, & \text{ if }\ \ \ \ \ \  (i,j)\in\{(k_{r},i_{r}),(k_{r},j_{r})\; | \; r  \in \Delta \}
\end{cases}
$$

Also, set $v_{\Sigma}:=v$. Note that $v_{\emptyset}=x$ and that $v_{\Delta}$ is $|\Delta|$-singular of index $2$ if $\Delta\neq \emptyset$.
